"terrifyingly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தெற்றிப்","parts":[{"text":"தெற்றி","lemma":"teṟṟi","gloss":"terrace"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"p","gloss":"increment"}],"gloss":"terrace"},{"surface":"பாவை","parts":[{"text":"பாவை","lemma":"pāvai","gloss":"doll"}],"gloss":"doll"},{"surface":"திணிமணல்","parts":[{"text":"திணி","lemma":"tiṇi","gloss":"dense"},{"text":"மணல்","lemma":"maṇal","gloss":"sand"}],"gloss":"dense sand"},{"surface":"அயரும்","parts":[{"text":"அயர்","lemma":"ayar","gloss":"play"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"aspect"}],"gloss":"playing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மென்தோள்","parts":[{"text":"மென்மை","lemma":"meṉmai","gloss":"soft"},{"text":"தோள்","lemma":"tōḷ","gloss":"shoulder"}],"gloss":"soft shoulders"},{"surface":"மகளிர்","parts":[{"text":"மகளிர்","lemma":"makaḷir","gloss":"women"}],"gloss":"women"},{"surface":"நன்று","parts":[{"text":"நன்று","lemma":"naṉṟu","gloss":"well"}],"gloss":"well"},{"surface":"புரப்ப","parts":[{"text":"புர","lemma":"pura","gloss":"protect"},{"text":"ப்ப","lemma":"ppa","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to protect"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"…","parts":[{"text":"…","lemma":"…","gloss":"…"}],"gloss":"…"},{"surface":"ண்ட","parts":[{"text":"ண்ட","lemma":"ṇṭa","gloss":"part of word"}],"gloss":"part of word"},{"surface":"பாசிலைக்","parts":[{"text":"பாசிலை","lemma":"pācilai","gloss":"green leaf"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"increment"}],"gloss":"green leaf"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கமழ்பூந்","parts":[{"text":"கமழ்","lemma":"kamaḻ","gloss":"fragrant"},{"text":"பூ","lemma":"pū","gloss":"flower"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"n","gloss":"increment"}],"gloss":"fragrant flower"},{"surface":"தும்பை","parts":[{"text":"தும்பை","lemma":"tumpai","gloss":"tumpai flower"}],"gloss":"tumpai flower"},{"surface":"நுதல்","parts":[{"text":"நுதல்","lemma":"nutal","gloss":"forehead"}],"gloss":"forehead"},{"surface":"அசைத்தோனே","parts":[{"text":"அசை","lemma":"acai","gloss":"tie/shake"},{"text":"த்து","lemma":"ttu","gloss":"having"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ōṉ","gloss":"he"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"he who tied"}]}],"literal":"Bright red kurali grass cool pond having been stirred / vāḷai fish otter daily prey obtaining / not obtaining striped snake with varāl fish getting confused / hostile crocodile with in turns moving / he of Aḻumpil unsubmissive one greatness always / victorious Kōcar assembly hall even in / in the public assembly that which is called to perish … particle for the companion / sharp-pointed mountain peak spear in the chest to pierce / life not leaving limit terrifyingly / terrace doll dense sand playing / soft-shouldered women well to protect / … green leaf / fragrant-flowered tumpai on forehead tied he.","translation":"The cool pond with bright red kurali grass is stirred up. The otter, seeking its daily prey of vāḷai fish, fails to catch it, and instead gets entangled with a striped snake and a varāl fish, moving back and forth in turns with a hostile crocodile. Such is the unsubmissive nature of the lord of Aḻumpil. Even in the assembly hall of the victorious Kōcar, his fame in the public assembly does not perish... For his companion, as the spear pierced his chest on the sharp-pointed mountain peak, while his life had not yet departed, terrifyingly, the soft-shouldered women who play with dolls on the dense sand of the terraces protected him well. He tied the fragrant-flowered green-leaved tumpai on his forehead.","modern":"ஒளிபொருந்திய சிவந்த குரலிச் செடிகள் நிறைந்த குளிர்ந்த குளம் கலங்குகிறது. நீர்நாய் தன் அன்றாட இரையாகிய வாளை மீனைப் பெற முயன்று, அது கிடைக்காமல், கோடுகளையுடைய பாம்போடும் வரால் மீனோடும் தடுமாறி, பகைமை கொண்ட முதலையோடு மாறி மாறிப் போராடித் திரும்புகிறது. அழும்பில் நாட்டின் தலைவனும் யாருக்கும் அடங்காதவனுமாகிய அவனது பெருமை எப்போதும் நிலைத்திருக்கும். வெற்றி பொருந்திய கோசர்களது அவைக்களத்திலும், பொதுமன்றத்திலும் அவனது புகழ் அழியாது... தன் தோழனுக்காக, கூர்மையான மலை உச்சியில் வேல் மார்பில் பாய்ந்து இயங்க, உயிர் பிரியாத நிலையில், அச்சம் தரும்படி திண்ணை மணலில் பாவை செய்து விளையாடும் மெல்லிய தோள்களைக் கொண்ட மகளிர் அவனை நன்றாகப் பாதுகாத்தனர். அவன் நறுமணம் வீசும் பசுமையான இலைகளையுடைய தும்பைப் பூவை நெற்றியில் சூடியுள்ளான்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Tumpai tiṇai (warfare) and the theme of Pāṇpāṭṭu (song of the bard). The bard sings in praise of the fierce and unsubmissive lord of Aḻumpil, comparing his relentless nature to an otter struggling in a pond with snakes, fish, and crocodiles. The opening image of the pond being stirred up represents the chaos and danger of the battlefield. Even in the assembly of the victorious Kōcar, the hero's fame remains undiminished. In the heat of battle on a mountain peak, a spear pierced his chest, yet before his life could depart, the soft-shouldered women who play on the sandy terraces protected and cared for him. He proudly wore the fragrant tumpai flower on his forehead, symbolizing his heroic stand.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.1],[1.1,1.6],[1.6,2.0],[2.0,2.7],[2.7,3.3],[3.3,3.8],[3.8,4.41],[4.41,4.87],[4.87,5.4],[5.4,6.2],[6.2,6.7],[6.7,7.12],[7.12,7.65],[7.65,8.6],[8.6,8.94],[8.94,9.74],[9.74,10.4],[10.4,10.8],[10.8,11.2],[11.2,11.89],[11.89,12.3],[12.3,13.23],[13.23,13.5],[13.5,14.2],[14.2,14.61],[14.61,14.82],[14.82,14.92],[14.92,15.5],[15.5,16.1],[16.1,16.85],[16.85,17.12],[17.4,17.56],[18.48,19.24],[19.24,19.38],[19.38,19.96],[20.13,20.39],[20.56,20.93],[20.93,21.12],[21.12,21.59],[21.59,22.08],[22.08,22.98],[22.98,23.18],[23.18,23.78],[23.78,24.31],[24.4,24.58],[24.58,24.98],[24.98,26.18],[26.18,26.38],[26.38,26.68],[26.68,26.98],[26.98,27.28]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.02],[1.1,1.6],[1.6,1.8],[1.8,2.7],[2.7,2.9],[2.9,3.7],[3.7,3.9],[3.9,4.22],[4.22,4.79],[4.79,5.5],[5.5,7.2],[7.2,8.25],[8.25,8.83],[8.83,9.3],[9.3,9.73],[9.73,10.7],[10.7,11.2],[11.2,11.6],[11.6,12.3],[12.3,13.5],[13.5,13.7],[13.7,14.28],[14.4,14.8],[14.8,15.8],[15.8,16.1],[16.1,16.43],[16.43,16.57],[16.57,17.3],[17.3,17.87],[17.87,19.0],[19.0,19.64],[19.7,20.0],[20.76,21.69],[21.